From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:08:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/57] Ask before losing changes when a file changes on disk

A tab with unsaved changes whose file changed on disk ignored the change,
and the next save overwrote it. Now a bar above the editor says
"<name> was changed on disk." with Reload, Compare and Keep mine; a
deleted file offers Keep mine only. Tabs without unsaved changes still
reload silently.

Each tab keeps the base: a content hash of the file as last loaded or
saved (hashed again only when its time or length changed). The file
watcher, switching to a tab, saving and session restore compare against
it, so our own saves never show the bar and a save never overwrites a
change nobody has seen: it shows the bar first, and saving again (or
Keep mine) accepts the version the bar was shown for. The session keeps
the base with the draft, so an unanswered bar survives a restart. A file
replaced by rename is watched again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

